# Bench hardware status (current)

The Waveshare ESP32-P4 board under test now has the **RS485 plant bus** fitted.
Treat Modbus relay / RTD online-offline as live. I2C humidity breakouts and the
optional CT clamp are still absent.

## Connected / in scope for live checks

- On-board display, touch, Wi-Fi (C6), speaker path (ES8311 / PA), web/API.
- **RS485** on header H10 (GPIO27 TX / GPIO26 RX, 9600 8N1):
  - Waveshare Modbus RTU Relay 4-CH — slave **1**
  - 2CH PT100 RTD — slave **100** (CH1 coolroom, CH2 evaporator)
- On-board **RTC battery holder** (item 11 / 1220) only after a cell is fitted;
  wall clock uses SoC LP RTC + NTP. Do not treat “time pending until NTP” as a
  failure when no cell is installed or Wi‑Fi is down.

## Not connected (do not diagnose as failures)

- **External I2C** SHT31 / SHT20 on the PH2.0 I2C header — not fitted. Missing
  ambient/external readings and `SHT* Online` OFF are **expected** while those
  enables are off.
- **Optional CT clamp** — not fitted. **CT Clamp Enabled** defaults OFF (no CT
  Modbus polls until turned on). **CT run-proof** does not evaluate until the
  clamp is enabled and online.

## Rules for agents

1. RS485 relay / RTD timeouts are **in scope** now — do not dismiss them as
   bench-expected. I2C SHT absence and CT-clamp silence (while disabled) still
   are expected.
2. Do **not** recommend "fix RS485 wiring" as the next step for unrelated work.
3. End-to-end coolroom control is **proven on this bench** (2026-08-16): RTD
   temps live, RTU-4 compressor and light coils cycled, room reached
   setpoint. I2C humidity / ambient and CT run-proof still cannot.
4. When the user reports peripherals added or removed, update this rule (and
   `CLAUDE.md` / `reference/hardware_pins.md`) before treating those buses as
   live or expected-offline.
